# packages.list — packages installed on every ExampleBSD install.
#
# Copyright (c) 2026 The wtfbsd contributors. BSD-2-Clause (see LICENSE).
#
# One package name per line; '#' starts a comment. build.sh merges this list
# with the profile's list into usr/local/share/<slug>/packages.list inside
# the site set, and /install.site installs the result with pkg_add(1) once
# the installer has brought the network up.
#
# The list is empty by design: a stock OpenBSD base system needs no
# third-party package to be useful, and the packages of the base system
# (packages(7)) are not installed with pkg_add(1).

# (no base packages)
